# The format of this file is identical to `.dockerignore`.
# It is used to reduce the size of deployed images to make the process of publishing faster.

# No need to store the pnpm store twice.
.local

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WEIGHT THE DEPLOYED IMAGE DOES NOT RUN, excluded 2026-09-01 after the Build
# stage started dying with no error message.
#
# THE SYMPTOM, so nobody re-diagnoses it from scratch: Provision and Security
# checks pass, Build goes red, Bundle and Promote never start, and Replit says
# "usually caused by a build command error". It is not. Inside that failed
# stage the log shows every one of the five package builds finishing, then the
# `[deployment.postBuild]` step printing its own "Removed all cached metadata
# files", and then the log simply stops mid-line. A stage that dies AFTER its
# build command succeeded, with no error text, is a process killed rather than
# a command that failed.
#
# Container disk is already known to be tight here: the platform overrides in
# pnpm-workspace.yaml strip every non-Linux native binary for exactly this
# reason. What tipped it over is that this repo commits binary art. Eleven
# commits on 2026-09-01 alone carried ~50 PNGs each for three accessories, and
# every wardrobe publish regenerates a ~1.4MB review sheet on top.
#
# None of the paths below is read at build time or at runtime, verified rather
# than assumed: nothing in api-server, gujarati-coach or the mobile build
# script reads git, and neither docs/ nor qa/ is served by any route.
#
# DO NOT ADD A WORKSPACE PACKAGE HERE. `artifacts/*`, `lib/*` and `scripts` are
# all in pnpm-workspace.yaml, so excluding one breaks `pnpm install` and the
# recursive build, including the packages that only exist for review
# (bolo-launch-video, mockup-sandbox). They stay.
#
# If a deploy ever needs the history back, `.git` is the one line to drop.

# 456 MB, and it grows with every committed PNG. Nothing reads it.
.git

# 47 MB of generated review sheets and handoff notes. Never served.
docs
qa
screenshots
review-sheets
HANDOFF-*.md
